    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on two high-upside matchups today, headlined by **Jacob Wilson** (74.08) and **Gunnar Henderson** (73.28). **Jacob Wilson** is our primary target against Cody Bradford; the matchup benefits from a significant SP skill advantage (+19%) and a favorable park factor (+10%), positioning him to provide elite production. Meanwhile, **Gunnar Henderson** faces Freddy Peralta in a dynamic platoon setup that generates a +14% boost. While Peralta is a competent arm, the combination of **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s aggressive profile and the potential for stolen bases\u2014supported by a slow pitcher delivery window\u2014makes him a cornerstone for our daily output. **Jackson Merrill** (69.57) also earns a strong recommendation, as his dynamic platoon advantage against Tanner Bibee outweighs the typical difficulties associated with facing a tough right-handed starter.\n\nThe decision to bench **Heliot Ramos** (45.00) remains the most difficult call of the morning. While he hovered near the 50-point threshold, he was ultimately nudged out by **Kyle Tucker** (51.47) and **Andy Pages** (47.54). Despite **Kyle Tucker** facing the challenging Logan Henderson, his raw talent and base projection provide a safer floor than **Heliot Ramos**, whose matchup against Dylan Cease carries too much volatility given Cease\u2019s high-strikeout profile. Our outfield depth is further tested by **Wade Meckler** (45.91) in a neutral-to-negative platoon spot, but his leadoff role secures his spot to ensure we maximize our plate appearance capacity.\n\nRisk mitigation is paramount today as we navigate a slate where most lineups remain \"Pending.\" We are particularly cautious regarding the matchups for **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker** against Logan Henderson, whose xERA of 2.84 presents a significant hurdle that drags down their individual scores. Furthermore, the reliance on assumed batting orders\u2014such as **Drake Baldwin** in the #2 hole\u2014introduces variance; should any of our hitters move down the order, their efficiency scores will adjust downward accordingly. We are monitoring all confirmed lineups closely, but as of now, the current configuration offers the optimal balance of stolen base potential and hitting efficiency.",
